# A2/A2.1/A2_12_past_tense.letz
# Source: PDF slide decks "L10 (Deel 1)/(Deel 2) a21lotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1, Lektioun 10).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma and participle verified against LOD.
# Grammar focus — this is the past-tense lesson:
#   - the passé composé = auxiliary + past participle, participle at the very END
#   - `hunn` for most verbs; `sinn` for verbs of MOVEMENT or CHANGE OF STATE,
#     plus the explicitly static `sinn` and `bleiwen`. Choosing the auxiliary is
#     the single highest-value habit here, so most fills blank it.
#   - inversion keeps the auxiliary in second position (Gëschter hunn ech ...)
#   - a subordinate clause sends the auxiliary to the end, AFTER the participle
#   - ongoing facts take the PRESENT in Luxembourgish, not the past
#     (`Ech wunnen zanter dräi Joer ...`) — a real interference error for English
#     and German speakers, so it is drilled explicitly.
# The deck also teaches the progressive `ech sinn am gaang ze ...`.

@lesson A2.12 "Past Tense"

# --- Talking about the past ---
@word d'Vergaangenheet = the past
@word virgëschter = the day before yesterday
@word hënt = last night
@word virdrun = before that
@word gläichzäiteg = at the same time
@word kuerz drop = shortly afterwards

# --- Nouns from the deck ---
@word d'Reunioun = the meeting
@word d'Ausbildung = the training
@word d'Nuechtiessen = the evening meal

# --- Verbs & expressions ---
@word gebuer sinn = to be born
@word pendelen = to commute
@word iwwernuechten = to stay overnight

# --- Past participles taking `hunn` ---
@word geschafft = worked
@word gesot = said
@word gemaach = done
@word geholl = taken
@word gelies = read
@word giess = eaten
@word gedronk = drunk
@word geschlof = slept
@word gehat = had
@word bruecht = brought
@word geduecht = thought
@word gefrot = asked
@word kaaft = bought
@word bezuelt = paid
@word geschriwwen = written
@word telefonéiert = telephoned
@word invitéiert = invited

# --- Past participles taking `sinn` ---
@word gefuer = driven
@word komm = arrived
@word gaangen = gone
@word gelaf = run
@word geflunn = flown
@word geschwomm = swum
@word gefall = fallen
@word opgestan = got up
@word gewiescht = been
@word bliwwen = stayed
@word geplënnert = moved house

